 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Gobbler is the term for a goose in bird watching. They' often easier to spot than geese, because they' smaller and skim over fields. Exactly. They also often have white head markings, so a white head on a bird usually means a gobbler. Very. Gobblers are often near water, and they' easy to spot. Starting with them gives you confidence before trying for more elusive birds. Try woodpiles or roosts at dusk. They often crowd together, and you' see lots of birds quickly.",
